mode: "100644"
text: "# Facebook 2026 — verified\n\n*Volatile. Re-verify quarterly.*\n\n## The shift: an AI discovery engine, not a Page-broadcast feed\nPage **organic reach has collapsed** to ~**1.65%** (range **1.6–5.9%** of followers) — but this isn't\nFacebook declining. The algorithm **fully shifted to proactive AI recommendation**: up to **35–50% of\nfeed views are \"unconnected\" content** from accounts users don't follow (\"Andromeda\"; UTIS Reels survey,\nJan 2026). It ranks in four steps — **Inventory → Signals → Predictions → Relevance Score** — and uses\n**NLP to read captions and video transcripts**, so Facebook now behaves like a **search/discovery\nengine**. Distribution depends on how well the AI understands your content, not how many follow you.\n\n## The signals that matter\n- **Saves & shares > likes/reactions** (the most powerful signals); meaningful comments (MSI),\n  long-form replies, shares to Stories, dwell time, and **watch time** rank highest.\n- **Engagement velocity in the first 30–60 min** is decisive — ~10 genuine comments in 30 min can\n  reach **3–5× more** people than the same spread over 24h. Reply to every comment early.\n- **Thematic consistency:** the algorithm scans your **last 9–12 posts** to tag the account. Scattered\n  topics confuse it → lower reach. **Focus ~2 core themes** (occasional off-topic is fine).\n\n## Surfaces + formats\n- **All videos are now Reels** (mid-2025). **Reels = highest reach/discovery** — pushed to non-followers\n  **by content category, not brand**; **Page Reels often beat Page posts 5–10×**. First 3 seconds,\n  retention, completion decide distribution.\n- **Photos = highest feed engagement**; **carousels** for storytelling. **Video is shared ~1,200% more**\n  than other formats. **Longer 3–8 min video** is now also boosted (\"time spent\").\n- **Links perform worst** (off-platform \"leaks\") → put the **link in the first comment** (or a native Shop).\n\n## Groups = the reach goldmine\n**1.8B monthly Group users.** Groups reach **~20–40% of members** vs **~1–6% for Pages** — a post in a\n10k-member Group reaches ~2,000–4,000 vs ~200–600 for a same-size Page. Group posts **rank higher** in\nFeed (community signal). The 2026 experience is **Groups-first**; Meta **algorithmically favors Groups**\n(they keep people on-platform) while **monetizing Pages via ads**. Building/owning Groups captures\nmaterially more reach.\n\n## Honest fit + caveats\n- **Small/specialized Pages can out-reach large ones** — large Pages are penalized for scale; niche\n  relevance wins.\n- **AI content is treated identically to human** (no penalty) — **but** low-quality AI-spam detection\n  is rising and there's an **authenticity premium** (BTS, personal stories, founder-led outperform).\n- **3B+ users, older-skewing**; great for **community, local, B2C, discovery**; weak for pure Page-feed\n  broadcasting. **Engagement-bait** (\"like & share\") is penalized. New: **creator affiliate program**\n  (Meta's TikTok-Shop answer) lets creators attach affiliate links to Reels.\n\n## The strategic pattern\n**Reels for unconnected discovery → Feed for connected depth/trust → Groups for community.** Reels gets\nyou in front of new people; Feed gives them a reason to stay and trust; Groups turns them into a community.\n"
